== the depth pass's choices are ADVERTISED by name ==
  [PASS] EchoJay Compressor mode: mode (clean|glue|punch|smooth, default clean) - compressor character, which reshapes attack, release and knee and adds gentle drive as it works: clean is a transparent VCA (the reference), glue is a slow soft bus compressor for making a mix cohere, punch is a fast aggressive FET for drums and bass, smooth is an opto with a programme-dependent release for vocals and anything delicate
  [PASS] EchoJay Compressor detector: detector (peak|rms, default rms) - what the detector measures: rms follows loudness and sounds like a fader being ridden (right for most material), peak catches every transient and is tighter on drums and bass
  [PASS] EchoJay Limiter mode: mode (transparent|punchy|clip, default transparent) - how it holds the ceiling: transparent is the clean lookahead limiter (use it on a master), punchy is faster with a touch of drive so a loud mix feels dense rather than just loud, clip is a hard ceiling - the loudest and most aggressive, and it ignores release and lookahead
  [PASS] EchoJay Gate mode: mode (gate|duck, default gate) - which side of the threshold gets attenuated: gate pulls down what is QUIETER than the threshold (cleaning up bleed and noise), duck pulls down what is LOUDER than it by range_db (holding something back whenever it gets loud). Everything else means the same in both
  [PASS] EchoJay 4-Band Compressor band1_mode: band1_mode (clean|glue|punch|smooth, default glue) - character for band 1 (below crossover1_hz), which reshapes its attack, release and knee and adds gentle drive as it works: clean is transparent, glue is slow and soft (right for a low band), punch is fast and aggressive (right for an air band), smooth has a programme-dependent release
  [PASS] EchoJay 4-Band Compressor detector: detector (peak|rms, default rms) - what every band's detector measures: rms follows loudness (right for multiband work, and what keeps the four bands comparable), peak catches transients and is tighter
  [PASS] EchoJay Stereo Width mode: mode (full|multiband, default full) - how width is applied: full is one width for the whole spectrum (the width knob), multiband splits the image at the two crossovers and applies width_low/width_mid/width_high independently - the classic mastering move is narrow lows, wide highs. In full mode the band widths are ignored; in multiband the single width is ignored. Mono fold-down stays exact in both
  [PASS] EchoJay Stereoizer mode: mode (haas|comb|dimension, default haas) - the widening character: haas displaces the image in time (haas_ms sets how far - broad and natural, the shipped sound), comb pushes an allpass-filtered copy of the centre into the sides (denser and more present, no pre-delay smear; haas_ms is ignored), dimension adds a slow detuned copy in the sides (lush, chorus-like movement, no comb colour; haas_ms is ignored). width scales the effect in every mode and the mono fold-down stays exact in every mode
  [PASS] EchoJay Gain mode: mode (stereo|mid_side, default stereo) - stereo is plain level + pan; mid_side adds independent gain on the mid (centre) and side (stereo difference) via mid_db/side_db - raise side_db to widen, lower it to narrow, lower mid_db to make room in the centre. level_db and pan still apply after it
  [PASS] EchoJay Compressor auto_release is advertised on/off: auto_release (on/off, default off) - release follows the programme: quick after a short transient, slower after a sustained passage that pulled deep. Use it when one release time cannot suit both
  [PASS] EchoJay Limiter true_peak is advertised on/off: true_peak (on/off, default off) - measure the peak BETWEEN samples, not just at them, so the ceiling still holds after a converter or a lossy encoder reconstructs the waveform. Turn it on for anything being mastered or exported; it costs a little loudness and no latency
  [PASS] EchoJay De-Esser auto_threshold is advertised on/off: auto_threshold (on/off, default off) - the threshold tracks a slow average of the band instead of sitting at a fixed level, so it de-esses relative to how loud the voice actually is and keeps working across a quiet verse and a loud chorus. While it is on, threshold_db is ignored - set range_db to control the amount
  [PASS] EchoJay Gain mono is advertised on/off: mono (on/off, default off) - sum the output to mono (both channels become the centre); the quick compatibility check, and a fade rather than a click
  [PASS] EchoJay Gain phase_left is advertised on/off: phase_left (on/off, default off) - invert the LEFT channel's polarity; use it to fix a flipped cable/mic - with mono on, inverting one side of an identical pair cancels to silence
  [PASS] EchoJay Gain phase_right is advertised on/off: phase_right (on/off, default off) - invert the RIGHT channel's polarity
